{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"e6d4813f22ddb02ab4ff047e0d9770a56e42fd25"},"timestamp":1533495031,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUzNDc3MjE4NjM=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2746","origin":"github"},"title":"Missing files in result from datalad get and drop for identical files","message":"#### What is the problem?\nIf in a given folder (including its subfolders), many files happen to have the same content, when doing a `datalad get`on the parent folder, the result only contains an entry for one of the files. The same is also taking place when using `datalad drop` on a folder with many identical files.\n#### What steps will reproduce the problem?\n1. Inside a dataset, create a folder. Inside that folder, create 2 copies of the same file with different names. Then create a subfolder and copy the previously created file in this subfolder with a different name.\n2. Use `datalad save` and `datalad publish` to send the data to any remote.\n3. Use `datalad drop` to drop the folder through the Python API. The result will only display one path for a dropped file as if only a single file was dropped although three files were dropped.\n3. Use `datalad get` on the first folder created in step one using the Python API. Looking at the result will only display one path for the file as they all share the same annexkey.\n#### What version of DataLad are you using?\nDatalad: datalad 0.10.1\nOS: Ubuntu 18.04.1 LTS\n#### Is there anything else that would be useful to know in this context?\nI am not sure if this is a limitation from git-annex or this this was a design choice. I understand that git-annex uses the files MD5 to generate the annex key so in reality, only one git-annex object is gotten and dropped each time. However, I believe it could be a nice addition for the user to have a list of paths when many files point to the same git-annex object.","files":null}]}